From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] services: services.listen, Linux pod listeners and SNMP agent
 through services, image services at day 0, passive BMP station

---
diff --git a/docs/module/services.md b/docs/module/services.md
index acbbcb1..aaeb711 100644
--- a/docs/module/services.md
+++ b/docs/module/services.md
@@ -130,3 +130,15 @@ snmp-server location lab-a
 
 The access level is spelled per platform -- `ro` on EOS, `RO` on IOS -- because
 these strings are written to the device verbatim.
+
+(services-bmp)=
+## BMP Monitoring Station (EOS and Junos)
+
+**services.bmp** (global/node dictionary, the platform extension) renders a passive BGP Monitoring Protocol station on the device, as day-0 configuration. It is rendered only on a node that runs the **bgp** module on a device declaring `services.bmp` (EOS, and the Junos devices except vSRX); on any other node the block is removed from the node data. There is no iBGP fallback.
+
+* **station** (string, required): DNS name or address of the BMP station, written to the device verbatim (no resolution by netlab).
+* **port** (int, default 50001): the TCP port the device listens on.
+* **mode** (default and only value: `passive`).
+* **name** (id, default `skyforge`): the station name on the device.
+* **failure_handling**: carried in node data for tooling; not rendered.
+* **enabled** (bool): `false` on a node removes the declaration for that node.
diff --git a/netsim/ansible/templates/initial/linux-kne.j2 b/netsim/ansible/templates/initial/linux-kne.j2
index 3cf9856..7fdb9c8 100644
--- a/netsim/ansible/templates/initial/linux-kne.j2
+++ b/netsim/ansible/templates/initial/linux-kne.j2
@@ -240,3 +240,14 @@ chmod +x /tmp/netlab-host-activity.sh
 pkill -f '/tmp/netlab-host-activity.sh' >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
 nohup /tmp/netlab-host-activity.sh >/var/log/netlab-host-activity.log 2>&1 &
 fi
+
+{#
+  PLATFORM-SPECIFIC (patch 40): a KNE pod never runs the image entrypoint (KNE replaces the command with `sleep`), so the
+  services the skyforge-linux-host image offers (Caldera agent launcher, opt-in listeners, iperf3, LLDP) are started from here,
+  the only script that runs in a KNE lab. The helper is idempotent (a warm reconfigure re-runs this script) and fails open; an
+  image without it (any non-platform linux image) is skipped. It reads its switches from the pod environment that patches 36
+  and 38 render, which `kubectl exec` inherits.
+#}
+if [ -x /usr/local/bin/skyforge-host-services.sh ]; then
+  nohup /usr/local/bin/skyforge-host-services.sh >/var/log/skyforge-host-services.log 2>&1 &
+fi
